{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Refined the proposed move to remove overlap with move 1 'spike'. Distinction: spike is a PLANNING-TIME experiment (before plan approval) that proves the mechanism/syntax and yields a decision; move 15 is an EXECUTION-TIME step the plan itself includes to prove the actual IMPLEMENTATION works before it enters the slow delivery loop.\n\nRefined proposal (pending approval):\n  \"15\": {\n      \"name\": \"out-of-loop proof\",\n      \"template\": \"Build an out-of-loop proof of {subject} into the plan — an execution step that confirms the implementation works via the fastest local run or manual probe against the real target, before it is committed to the slow delivery loop.\",\n      \"applies_when\": [\"T15\"],\n  }\n\nSupersedes the earlier draft template ('Prove {subject} with the fastest out-of-loop experiment ... before committing it to the slow delivery loop'), which read as a planning-time activity and overlapped spike."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784919283159287001,"uuid":"40f70aaa-ca01-4f53-a251-d9d83029cec0"}